Ritemark Menu Cleanup: hide VS Code dev features (chat, debug, go menu, emmet)
Sprint 1+: Original menu cleanup.
Sprint 55: Rebased onto VS Code 1.117.0
  - Optional-guard fixes around defaultChatAgent (upstream now allows null)
  - Removal of generic top-level Go / Run / Terminal surfaces
  - Hiding upstream chat status/titlebar entry points
  - Disabling chat view registration in favor of Ritemark-owned surfaces
  - Removing classic Edit-menu items that conflict with the document-first UI
  - Added MenuId.MenubarViewMenuAdvanced wiring (for View > Advanced submenu)
Sprint 132 (Ritemark 2.0, after Windows round 1, 2026-10-18):
  - No Run entry in the View menu (a fresh profile showed one)
  - No Chat entry for the panel's chat view; the View menu's Copilot Chat
    opens it as a tab instead (patch 007)
Sprint 134 (Ritemark 2.0, step 3; R21, #456):
  - All commands no longer offers VS Code's developer and debugging commands:
    one filter of command IDs and ID prefixes where getCommandPicks returns
    (commandsQuickAccess.ts, isHiddenFromRitemarkPalette), so search, similar
    commands and recently used never show them. They stay registered, so their
    menus and shortcuts still run them. The list is research/palette-audit.md §7.
    Test: contrib/quickaccess/test/browser/ritemarkPalettePolicy.test.ts.
